e_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106500","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106500","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106500.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106500.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-26T16:30:23Z"},"body":"Closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12418\r\nCloses https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98312\r\n\r\n[2025-05-19-00.webm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e069363-6942-40a0-801b-baf2cbd4ceaa)\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\nFindInFiles is inherently tied to the ScriptEditor as that is where the results are opened. With the current implementation you can only FindInFiles when the Script tab is open (and use the keyboard shortcut only when a file is open).\r\n\r\nTo make this more global I have left all the connection in ScriptEditor, but have exposed FindInFilesDialog as a singleton as that is the entry point for triggering the action.\r\n\r\nIn the proposal I have suggested making changes to the EditorLog as well, but that was starting to feel like scope creep and has been undone. I have opened a proposal (https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12462) specifically for it to gather more discussion instead.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n- Make ScriptEditor expose open_find_in_files_dialog to replace `_on_find_in_files_requested` to allow opening from anywhere\r\n- Add FindInFiles to EditorNode as a keyboard shortcut, command, and project menu option\r\n- Change all find_in_files commands/shortcuts to be editor/find_in_files","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use